@startuml Enhanced_DSS_State_Diagram
!theme plain

title Enhanced Decision Support System - Talent Request Lifecycle State Diagram
note top : "Complete state transitions with Enhanced DSS integration and critical competency handling"

[*] --> Draft : User starts creating request

state Draft {
  Draft : User configuring request
  Draft : - Adding competencies
  Draft : - Setting weights (0-100%)
  Draft : - Marking critical competencies
  Draft : - Configuring veto threshold (60-100%)
  Draft : - Specifying location preferences
}

Draft --> ValidationInProgress : User submits request
note on link : store() called with form data

state ValidationInProgress {
  ValidationInProgress : TalentRequestRequest validation
  ValidationInProgress : - Weight distribution check (≤100% total)
  ValidationInProgress : - Critical competency ratio (≤70%)
  ValidationInProgress : - Veto threshold range (60-100%)
  ValidationInProgress : - Required field validation
  ValidationInProgress : - Business rule compliance
}

ValidationInProgress --> ValidationFailed : Validation errors found
ValidationInProgress --> PendingAdmin : Validation successful

ValidationFailed --> Draft : User corrects errors
note on link : Redirect back with error messages

state PendingAdmin {
  PendingAdmin : Awaiting admin review
  PendingAdmin : - Request visible in admin dashboard
  PendingAdmin : - Enhanced DSS ready for processing
  PendingAdmin : - Basic SAW available for comparison
}

PendingAdmin --> DSSProcessing : Admin views request details
note on link : show() triggers DSS algorithms

state DSSProcessing {
  DSSProcessing : Enhanced DSS Algorithm Execution
  --
  DSSProcessing : 1. Extract & validate competencies
  DSSProcessing : 2. Normalize weights (competency: 85%, location: 15%)
  DSSProcessing : 3. Filter qualified talents (mandatory requirements)
  DSSProcessing : 4. Apply veto thresholds (critical competencies)
  DSSProcessing : 5. Normalize performance values (min-max)
  DSSProcessing : 6. Calculate SAW scores with bonuses
  DSSProcessing : 7. Generate confidence & sensitivity analysis
  --
  DSSProcessing : Parallel: Basic SAW for comparison
}

DSSProcessing --> NoQualifiedTalents : No talents meet criteria
DSSProcessing --> ResultsAvailable : Qualified talents found

state NoQualifiedTalents {
  NoQualifiedTalents : No matching talents
  NoQualifiedTalents : - All talents eliminated by veto thresholds
  NoQualifiedTalents : - Insufficient competency levels
  NoQualifiedTalents : - Location compatibility issues
}

NoQualifiedTalents --> RejectedByAdmin : Admin rejects due to unrealistic requirements
NoQualifiedTalents --> PendingAdmin : Admin modifies criteria and retries

state ResultsAvailable {
  ResultsAvailable : DSS results ready for admin review
  ResultsAvailable : - Enhanced DSS rankings (up to 10 talents)
  ResultsAvailable : - Basic SAW comparison (up to 5 talents)
  ResultsAvailable : - Score breakdowns and methodology
  ResultsAvailable : - Confidence indicators
  ResultsAvailable : - Sensitivity analysis for top candidates
}

ResultsAvailable --> TalentSelection : Admin reviews results

state TalentSelection {
  TalentSelection : Admin decision making
  TalentSelection : - Review Enhanced DSS recommendations
  TalentSelection : - Compare with Basic SAW results
  TalentSelection : - Analyze score contributions
  TalentSelection : - Check confidence levels
  TalentSelection : - Consider business factors
}

TalentSelection --> RejectedByAdmin : Admin decides to reject request
TalentSelection --> PendingTalent : Admin selects and assigns talents

RejectedByAdmin --> [*] : Request lifecycle ends
note on link : reject() method called

state PendingTalent {
  PendingTalent : Awaiting talent responses
  PendingTalent : - Assigned talents notified
  PendingTalent : - Individual assignment statuses tracked
  PendingTalent : - Parallel responses possible

  state "Individual Assignment States" as IAS {
    state Notified
    state Reviewing
    state Accepted
    state Rejected

    Notified --> Reviewing : Talent views assignment
    Reviewing --> Accepted : Talent accepts
    Reviewing --> Rejected : Talent declines
  }
}

PendingTalent --> Approved : At least one talent accepts
PendingTalent --> RejectedByTalent : All assigned talents reject

state Approved {
  Approved : Active talent assignment
  Approved : - Project can commence
  Approved : - Talent(s) confirmed for project
  Approved : - Assignment tracking active
}

state RejectedByTalent {
  RejectedByTalent : All talents declined
  RejectedByTalent : - No available talent assignments
  RejectedByTalent : - Admin can reassign or close request
}

RejectedByTalent --> TalentSelection : Admin selects different talents
RejectedByTalent --> [*] : Admin closes request permanently

Approved --> Completed : Project finished successfully
Approved --> Cancelled : Project cancelled or terminated

state Completed {
  Completed : Project successfully completed
  Completed : - Final project delivery
  Completed : - Performance evaluation
  Completed : - Historical record maintained
}

state Cancelled {
  Cancelled : Project cancelled or terminated
  Cancelled : - Reasons documented
  Cancelled : - Talent assignments released
  Cancelled : - Historical record maintained
}

Completed --> [*] : Request lifecycle ends
Cancelled --> [*] : Request lifecycle ends

' Additional state annotations for Enhanced DSS features
note right of DSSProcessing
  **Enhanced DSS Features:**

  - Critical competency veto thresholds
  - Progressive bonus system (up to 20%)
  - Location intelligence scoring
  - Mathematical SAW compliance
  - Confidence scoring (multi-factor)
  - Sensitivity analysis (top candidates)
  - Academic weight validation
  - Edge case handling (zero-range normalization)
end note

note left of ValidationInProgress
  **Enhanced Validation Rules:**

  Business Rules:
  - Maximum 70% critical competencies
  - Veto threshold: 60-100%
  - Weight distribution: ≤100% total
  - Single competency: ≤100%
  - Extreme dominance warning: >90%

  Academic Compliance:
  - SAW methodology standards
  - Mathematical bounds checking
  - Zero-weight scenario support
end note

note bottom of ResultsAvailable
  **Dual Algorithm Output:**

  Enhanced DSS (10 results):
  - Veto threshold filtering
  - Critical competency bonuses
  - Advanced location scoring
  - Confidence indicators

  Basic SAW (5 results):
  - Standard SAW implementation
  - Simple competency scoring
  - Basic location compatibility
  - Comparison baseline
end note

@enduml
